-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ב/2 (17.8.2021), העסקת עו"ה, עובדי בעלות, בבתי ספר לחינוך
-- מיוחד מוכרים שאינם רשמיים, בהתאם לרפורמת אופק חדש בשנה"ל תשפ"ב.
-- Applying the Ofek Hadash reform from תשפ"ב to teaching employees of the
-- owners of recognised unofficial special-education schools: the owner's
-- and the Ministry's duties, who joins, the work week, part-time and
-- over-100% employment, mothers' and age hours, principals and deputies,
-- activity hours, leaving the reform, promotion, counsellors, the grade and
-- the role bonuses, the salary advances, the time clock, and the annexed
-- commitment, forms and conversion of salary.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תשפ"ב/2 העסקת עובדי הוראה בבתי ספר לחינוך מיוחד מוכרים שאינם רשמיים באופק חדש`

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 The letterhead, the date and the reference number; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 The circular's number, the addressees (owners of recognised unofficial special-education schools not yet in Ofek Hadash), the greeting and the subject line; no rule.

-- Time in the regulative rules is counted in DAYS from 17 August 2021 (day
-- 0), the circular's date, unless a rule says otherwise.
`17 August 2021` MEANS 0
`30 August 2021` MEANS 13

-- The owner of the school (הבעלות) is the employer of its teaching
-- employees; common.l4 names it `the local authority or owning body`.

DECLARE `reform action` IS ONE OF
    `submit the commitment to join Ofek Hadash through the portal`
    `instruct teachers without a file to open an online teaching-employee file`
    `transfer the salary interface to the Ministry's contractor`
    `pay salary by the Ofek Hadash grade and deduct the advances`
    `pay the Ofek Hadash advance` HAS `advance paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay and deduct salary by the time clock`
    `employ beyond the limits`
    `teach more than two role bonuses' worth`

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- akn:art_1/p1 akn:art_1/p2 akn:art_1/p3 akn:art_1/p4 akn:art_1/p5 Background: the State's undertaking in HCJ 148/18 to equalise teaching resources from תש"ף, the inter-ministerial team and its report; no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p6 Background: Ofek Hadash terms were applied to recognised unofficial special-education schools from תש"ף; the rules that follow are encoded below.
-- akn:art_1/p8 akn:art_1/p9 The circular's purpose, following circular תש"ף/1; no rule.

@desc The decisions ¶7 reserves to the Ministry.
DECLARE `reserved decision` IS ONE OF
    `approving a teaching employee's joining Ofek Hadash`
    `setting the Ofek Hadash grade`
    `converting the salary`
    `setting the education rank`
    `setting the seniority in teaching`

@ref akn:art_1/p7
GIVEN d IS A `reserved decision`
GIVETH A Party
DECIDE `who decides` d IS
    `the Ministry of Education`

§§ `2 תחומי אחריות ביישום הרפורמה`

-- akn:art_2__para_2-1/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-1/p2 The headings "2.1 שלב ראשון" and "actions by the owner"; no rule.

-- 2.1.1: until the regulations are amended, the owner commits to apply the
-- reform; the text of the commitment is annex א; it is submitted only
-- through the portal, by 30.8.2021.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p5 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p6 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p7
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `submitting the commitment to join` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `submit the commitment to join Ofek Hadash through the portal`
    WITHIN `30 August 2021`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ב/2 §2.1.1: the commitment to join Ofek Hadash for תשפ\"ב is due by 30.8.2021"

-- 2.1.2: the owner checks that the teachers' data in the "נתוני כח אדם
-- בהוראה" report are current (א), and has teachers not yet reported open an
-- online file urgently, following the circular on candidates (ב).
@desc The teaching employees' data §2.1.2א asks the owner to check.
DECLARE `teacher data item` IS ONE OF
    `academic and pedagogical education`
    `seniority, military and national service included`
    `in-service training bonuses and double degree`

@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_a
GIVEN `the data are current` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner must have the data updated through the district` `the data are current` IF
    NOT `the data are current`

@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4__cls_1
GIVEN `teachers not yet reported` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `having unreported teachers open a file` `teachers not yet reported` IS
    IF `teachers not yet reported` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `instruct teachers without a file to open an online teaching-employee file`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 2.1.3: the owner identifies the teachers who meet the conditions of §3.
-- 2.1.4: they are employed on Ofek Hadash pay and work week (§4).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employed on Ofek Hadash pay and work week` t IF
    `joins Ofek Hadash` t

-- akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4/p2 The heading "actions by the principal"; no rule.

-- The principal's actions: guide the teachers in opening files (cited with
-- 2.1.2ב above), set the timetable by the Ofek work week (§4), and place
-- every teacher, in or out of the reform, in the placement system.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4__cls_2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4__cls_3
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal places the teacher in the placement system` t IF
    TRUE

-- 2.2: stage two. The owner transfers to the Ministry's contractor the
-- interface of the salary it paid in the month asked for; the Ministry sets
-- the grade and converts; the owner then pays by the grade from the joining
-- date and deducts the advances (§15).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-2/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2
GIVEN `the grade has been set` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `stage two` `the grade has been set` IS
    IF `the grade has been set`
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `pay salary by the Ofek Hadash grade and deduct the advances`
    ELSE PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `transfer the salary interface to the Ministry's contractor`

-- The Ministry's actions: check each teacher against the conditions and
-- decide joining, set the grade, compute the school's Ofek profile, and
-- reimburse the owner — which it cannot do without the placement system
-- updated to the Ofek week and the salary interface transferred.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p5 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p6 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p7 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p8 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p9
GIVEN `placement system updated to the Ofek week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `salary interface transferred`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ministry can reimburse the owner for the reform` `placement system updated to the Ofek week` `salary interface transferred` IF
        `placement system updated to the Ofek week`
    AND `salary interface transferred`

§§ `3 תנאי ההצטרפות`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-1/p1 The heading "3.1 הגדרות"; no rule.

@desc A teaching employee of the owner, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `Ofek teacher` HAS
    `years of recognised actual teaching`         IS A NUMBER  @desc seniority recognised for actual teaching, with the State or another employer; an internship year, military or national service in teaching does not count
    `years of seniority`                          IS A NUMBER  @desc seniority in teaching for salary
    `academic`                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc holds an academic degree, or a salary grade the Ministry's teaching-staff division approved as equivalent
    `certified to teach`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc holds a teaching certificate or another certification the Ministry recognises
    `position fraction`                           IS A NUMBER
    `school joined Ofek Hadash`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed the commitment to complete a degree`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the exceptions committee`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `an intern`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a health or arts-therapy professional`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc occupational therapy, physiotherapy, speech therapy, or therapy through visual art, movement, drama, music, bibliotherapy or psychodrama

-- 3.1.1-3.1.2.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-1
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new teaching employee` t IF
    t's `years of recognised actual teaching` EQUALS 0

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-2
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing teaching employee` t IF
    t's `years of recognised actual teaching` GREATER THAN 0

`a third of a position` MEANS 1 DIVIDED BY 3

-- 3.2.1: an existing academic teacher in a school that joined joins when
-- certified and employed at a third of a position or more. An uncertified
-- one may ask the exceptions committee (annex ב); the committee's approval
-- is read as standing in for the certificate only.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p4 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p5 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p6 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p7 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p8 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p9
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing academic teacher joins` t IF
        t's `position fraction` AT LEAST `a third of a position`
    AND (t's `certified to teach` OR t's `approved by the exceptions committee`)

-- 3.2.1 ¶10-11: uncertified and below 25 years: no promotion until
-- certified (see §12.2.2 and F-2021-22_tashpab_02-e).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p10 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p11
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `barred from promotion until certified under section 3.2.1` t IF
        (NOT t's `certified to teach`)
    AND t's `years of seniority` LESS THAN 25

-- akn:art_3__para_3-3/p1 The heading "3.3 existing non-academic teachers"; no rule.

-- 3.3.1-3.3.2: an existing non-academic teacher with up to 27 years (27
-- included) joins only after signing the commitment to complete a degree
-- within 4 years (annex ג); one with 28 years or more joins without it.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-2
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing non-academic teacher joins` t IF
        t's `years of seniority` AT LEAST 28
    OR  t's `signed the commitment to complete a degree`

-- 3.3.3: the owner follows up the commitment.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-3
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner must follow up the commitment` t IF
        t's `signed the commitment to complete a degree`
    AND (NOT t's `academic`)

-- 3.3.4: completing the degree within 4 years of joining the reform earns
-- the salary difference retroactively from the joining date; later, a move
-- to the academic table without arrears. F-2021-22_tashpab_02-f: the
-- 4-year window and the date of the arrears are stated differently in
-- 3.3.1 and annex ג.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-4 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-4/p2
GIVEN `months from joining to the degree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `arrears from joining under section 3.3.4` `months from joining to the degree` IF
    `months from joining to the degree` AT MOST 48

-- 3.4: a new academic teacher in a school that joined joins when certified
-- and employed at a third of a position or more (half a position in regular
-- education, which this circular does not govern).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p4 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p5 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p6 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p7
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new teacher joins` t IF
        t's `academic`
    AND t's `position fraction` AT LEAST `a third of a position`
    AND (t's `certified to teach` OR t's `approved by the exceptions committee`)

-- akn:art_3__para_3-5/p1 The heading "3.5 interns"; no rule.

-- 3.5.1: interns in a school that joined are employed only under the
-- reform; an internship year is recognised only at a third of a position.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-1
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship year is recognised` t IF
        t's `an intern`
    AND t's `position fraction` AT LEAST `a third of a position`

-- 3.5.2: at most two years of internship, in which the degree and the
-- certificate are completed, or the intern may not go on under the reform.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-2
GIVEN `years of internship` IS A NUMBER, `completed the degree and the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the intern may go on under the reform` `years of internship` `completed the degree and the certificate` IF
        `years of internship` AT MOST 2
    OR  `completed the degree and the certificate`

-- 3.5.3: what the internship counts for.
@desc The kinds of seniority §3.5.3 names.
DECLARE `seniority purpose` IS ONE OF
    `seniority for salary`
    `the minimum period for promotion`
    `seniority for tenure`
    `seniority for the jubilee grant`
    `seniority for the recuperation allowance`

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-3
GIVEN p IS A `seniority purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship counts for` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `seniority for salary` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the minimum period for promotion` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- 3.6: a substitute on weekly hours (not single hours) is employed on the
-- characteristics of the teacher replaced.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-6/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-6/p2
GIVEN `employed on weekly hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `replaced teacher in the reform` IS A BOOLEAN, `otherwise in the reform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substitute is employed in the reform` `employed on weekly hours` `replaced teacher in the reform` `otherwise in the reform` IS
    IF `employed on weekly hours` THEN `replaced teacher in the reform` ELSE `otherwise in the reform`

-- Who joins, put together (§§3.2-3.4, and §3.5.1 for interns).
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `joins Ofek Hadash` t IF
        t's `school joined Ofek Hadash`
    AND (    t's `an intern`
         OR (`a new teaching employee` t AND `a new teacher joins` t)
         OR (`an existing teaching employee` t AND t's `academic` AND `an existing academic teacher joins` t)
         OR (`an existing teaching employee` t AND (NOT t's `academic`) AND `an existing non-academic teacher joins` t))

§§ `4 מבנה שבוע העבודה למורים ברפורמה`

@desc A weekly structure of work: total, frontal, individual and stay hours.
DECLARE `work week` HAS
    `weekly hours`     IS A NUMBER
    `frontal hours`    IS A NUMBER
    `individual hours` IS A NUMBER
    `stay hours`       IS A NUMBER

-- 4.1: a full position is five working days, also in six-day schools.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-1
`working days of a full position` MEANS 5

@desc The special-education schools §4 distinguishes.
DECLARE `school structure` IS ONE OF
    `a primary school of grades 1-6, 1-8 or 1-9`
    `a multi-stage school`
    `a secondary school`

-- 4.2-4.3: which week applies. In a primary school every teacher (existing
-- teachers on a 30-hour or a kept 24-hour base included) works the primary
-- week (4.4); in a multi-stage school, grades 1-6 the primary week and
-- grades 7-12 the secondary week (4.6).
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2 akn:art_4__para_4-2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-2/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-3 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p4
GIVEN s IS A `school structure`, `teaches in grades 1-6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the primary week applies` s `teaches in grades 1-6` IF
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `a primary school of grades 1-6, 1-8 or 1-9` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a multi-stage school` THEN `teaches in grades 1-6`
    WHEN `a secondary school` THEN FALSE

-- akn:art_4__para_4-4/p1 The heading "4.4 the work week in a primary special-education school"; no rule.

-- 4.4: 36 hours: 26 frontal, 5 individual (groups of up to 3, content set
-- by the principal), 5 stay hours, of them up to 2 in work meetings.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-2 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-3 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_1
`the primary teacher's week` MEANS `work week` 36 26 5 5

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_1
`work meetings in the primary week, at most` MEANS 2

-- The rest of the stay hours: the activities listed, and the link to the
-- detailed table.
@desc The activities §§4.4.4(2) and 4.6.4(2) list for the rest of the stay hours.
DECLARE `stay activity` IS ONE OF
    `adapting the curriculum and the environment to the pupil`
    `individual meetings with parents`
    `checking work and tests`
    `preparing for and taking part in committees`
    `planning and guiding the special-education assistants`
    `coordinating with outside bodies for the pupil's inclusion`
    `coordinating for educational continuity`
    `work meetings`

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p5 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p6 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p7 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p8 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p9 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p10 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p11 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p12 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p13 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p5 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p6 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p7 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p8 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p9 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p10 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p11
GIVEN a IS A `stay activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a stay hour may be spent on` a IF
    TRUE

-- 4.5: health and arts-therapy professionals in a primary school: as a
-- teacher, but 3 individual and 7 stay hours, 2 of which may be spent
-- travelling between institutions.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-5 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p5
`the primary health professional's week` MEANS `work week` 36 26 3 7

`stay hours that may be spent travelling` MEANS 2

-- akn:art_4__para_4-6/p1 The heading "4.6 the work week in a secondary school"; no rule.

-- 4.6: 36 hours: 23 frontal, 4 individual, 9 stay, of them up to 4 in work
-- meetings.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-2 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-3 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_1
`the secondary teacher's week` MEANS `work week` 36 23 4 9

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_1
`work meetings in the secondary week, at most` MEANS 4

-- 4.7 and the link after it: health professionals in a secondary school: 2
-- individual and 11 stay hours, 2 of which for travelling.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-7 akn:art_4__para_4-7/p2 akn:art_4/p1 akn:art_4/p2 akn:art_4/p3
`the secondary health professional's week` MEANS `work week` 36 23 2 11

GIVEN s IS A `school structure`, `teaches in grades 1-6` IS A BOOLEAN, `health professional` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the full-position work week` s `teaches in grades 1-6` `health professional` IS
    IF `the primary week applies` s `teaches in grades 1-6`
    THEN IF `health professional` THEN `the primary health professional's week` ELSE `the primary teacher's week`
    ELSE IF `health professional` THEN `the secondary health professional's week` ELSE `the secondary teacher's week`

-- Every week adds up to its 36 hours.
GIVEN w IS A `work week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the week adds up` w IF
    w's `frontal hours` PLUS w's `individual hours` PLUS w's `stay hours` EQUALS w's `weekly hours`

#ASSERT all `the week adds up`
            (LIST `the primary teacher's week`, `the primary health professional's week`,
                  `the secondary teacher's week`, `the secondary health professional's week`)

§§ `5 העסקה בחלקיות משרה ברפורמה`

-- 5.1-5.2: a teacher under the reform is employed at a third of a position
-- or more; a health professional may be employed below it.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-1 akn:art_5__para_5-2
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the position meets the floor` t IF
        t's `a health or arts-therapy professional`
    OR  t's `position fraction` AT LEAST `a third of a position`

-- 5.3: a part-time position is cut from each kind of hour in proportion.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-3
GIVEN w IS A `work week`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the part-time week` w f IS
    `work week` (w's `weekly hours` TIMES f) (w's `frontal hours` TIMES f) (w's `individual hours` TIMES f) (w's `stay hours` TIMES f)

-- 5.3 ¶2: below a third, a health professional — or a teacher of a required
-- subject approved by the teaching-staff division — on three frontal hours
-- or fewer ("single frontal hours") works only those hours; the position is
-- their share of the base.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-3/p2
GIVEN `frontal hours` IS A NUMBER, `base of the position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position on single frontal hours` `frontal hours` `base of the position` IS
    `frontal hours` DIVIDED BY `base of the position`

GIVEN `frontal hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `single frontal hours` `frontal hours` IF
    `frontal hours` AT MOST 3

-- 5.4: at most two schools, and at most 100% in all employments, one school
-- or two; not for health professionals or a subject the division allows in
-- more schools. F-2021-22_tashpab_02-a: §6 allows more than 100%.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-4
GIVEN `number of schools` IS A NUMBER, `total position` IS A NUMBER, `exempt from section 5.4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5.4 permits the employment` `number of schools` `total position` `exempt from section 5.4` IF
        `exempt from section 5.4`
    OR (`number of schools` AT MOST 2 AND `total position` AT MOST 1)

-- 5.5: work below a third of a position does not count toward the required
-- period (פז"נ) for promotion.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-5
GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period counts toward promotion` f IF
    f AT LEAST `a third of a position`

§§ `6 העסקה מעל 100% משרה ברפורמה`

-- 6.1: as a rule up to 100%. 6.2: exceptionally, for teachers (not
-- principals or first deputies), by the system's needs and the criteria.
@desc The facts §6.2's criteria ask about.
DECLARE `over-position request` HAS
    `teaches a required subject`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc science, English, mathematics or physical education
    `teacher shortage in the area`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `remote locality, hard to recruit`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `additional hours are frontal only`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours a day`                                IS A NUMBER  @desc frontal, individual and stay hours together, on the longest day
    `hours a week`                               IS A NUMBER
    `a principal or first deputy`                IS A BOOLEAN

-- The reading adopted (F-2021-22_tashpab_02-b): the first three criteria
-- are the needs, any of which may ground the request; the last two are
-- conditions every request meets.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1 akn:art_6__para_6-2 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p2 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p3 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p4 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p5 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p6
GIVEN r IS AN `over-position request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the request meets the criteria` r IF
        (NOT r's `a principal or first deputy`)
    AND (r's `teaches a required subject` OR r's `teacher shortage in the area` OR r's `remote locality, hard to recruit`)
    AND r's `additional hours are frontal only`
    AND r's `hours a day` AT MOST 8.5
    AND r's `hours a week` AT MOST 42

-- The other reading: every listed criterion together.
GIVEN r IS AN `over-position request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the request meets every criterion` r IF
        (NOT r's `a principal or first deputy`)
    AND r's `teaches a required subject`
    AND r's `teacher shortage in the area`
    AND r's `remote locality, hard to recruit`
    AND r's `additional hours are frontal only`
    AND r's `hours a day` AT MOST 8.5
    AND r's `hours a week` AT MOST 42

`a mathematics teacher in a central town` MEANS
    `over-position request` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 8 40 FALSE

`the two readings of the criteria decide one request differently` MEANS
        `the request meets the criteria` `a mathematics teacher in a central town`
    AND (NOT `the request meets every criterion` `a mathematics teacher in a central town`)
#ASSERT `the two readings of the criteria decide one request differently`

-- 6.3: the placement system allows up to 117%; 6.4: beyond 117% the
-- teaching-staff division's head office approves, through the entitlements
-- system. The link to the procedure follows.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-3 akn:art_6__para_6-4 akn:art_6/p1
GIVEN `total position` IS A NUMBER, r IS AN `over-position request`, `approved by the head office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6 permits the employment` `total position` r `approved by the head office` IF
        `total position` AT MOST 1
    OR (`the request meets the criteria` r AND `total position` AT MOST 1.17)
    OR (`the request meets the criteria` r AND `approved by the head office`)

-- F-2021-22_tashpab_02-a: a teacher at 110% in one school, on an approved
-- request: §6 permits it and §5.4 does not.
`sections 5.4 and 6 decide 110% in one school differently` MEANS
        `section 6 permits the employment` 1.1 `a mathematics teacher in a central town` FALSE
    AND (NOT `section 5.4 permits the employment` 1 1.1 FALSE)
#ASSERT `sections 5.4 and 6 decide 110% in one school differently`

§§ `7 עו"ה אם`

-- 7.1: entitlement to a mother's position follows the takanon: a teaching
-- employee employed at 79% or more of her position (the child's age is the
-- takanon's, an input here).
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-1 akn:art_7__para_7-1/p2
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `a mother under the takanon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a mother the takanon's rule on a mother's position covers
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to a mother's position` `position fraction` `a mother under the takanon` IF
        `a mother under the takanon`
    AND `position fraction` AT LEAST 0.79

-- 7.2: one frontal and one stay hour less than the regular week; the
-- week tables carry it.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-2 akn:art_7__para_7-2/p2
GIVEN w IS A `work week`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the mother's week` w IS
    `work week` (w's `weekly hours` MINUS 2) (w's `frontal hours` MINUS 1) (w's `individual hours`) (w's `stay hours` MINUS 1)

-- 7.3: after maternity leave, at 90% or more: for four months, one hour a
-- day off the stay hours (five a week), §7.2 not applying meanwhile.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-3
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `months since the maternity leave ended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7.3 gives the nursing hour` `position fraction` `months since the maternity leave ended` IF
        `position fraction` AT LEAST 0.90
    AND `months since the maternity leave ended` LESS THAN 4

`nursing hours a week` MEANS 5

-- 7.4: such a teacher at 79% to 90% gets the mother's reduction of §7.2.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-4
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7.4 gives the mother's reduction` `position fraction` IF
        `position fraction` AT LEAST 0.79
    AND `position fraction` AT MOST 0.90

-- 7.5: never both at once. F-2021-22_tashpab_02-c: at exactly 90% both
-- 7.3 and 7.4 apply.
`at 90% sections 7.3 and 7.4 both apply` MEANS
        `section 7.3 gives the nursing hour` 0.90 1
    AND `section 7.4 gives the mother's reduction` 0.90
#ASSERT `at 90% sections 7.3 and 7.4 both apply`

-- The reading adopted: "עד 90%" stops short of 90%, so at 90% the nursing
-- hour of 7.3 applies.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-5
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `months since the maternity leave ended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the reduction after maternity leave` `position fraction` `months since the maternity leave ended` IS
    IF `section 7.3 gives the nursing hour` `position fraction` `months since the maternity leave ended`
    THEN "the nursing hour"
    ELSE IF `section 7.4 gives the mother's reduction` `position fraction`
         THEN "the mother's reduction"
         ELSE "none"

§§ `8 מורים הזכאים לשעות גיל`

-- 8.1: the age of eligibility is as before the reform (an input).
@desc A teacher's age-hours facts.
DECLARE `age-hours teacher` HAS
    `age for age hours` IS A NUMBER  @desc the age as the pre-reform rules count it for age hours (section 8.1)
    `existing`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc an existing teaching employee (section 3.1.2); otherwise new (3.1.1)

@desc What §§8.2-8.4 give: the reduction for a full position and the base it leaves.
DECLARE `age reduction` HAS
    `frontal hours off`    IS A NUMBER
    `individual hours off` IS A NUMBER
    `base after reduction` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_8__para_8-1 akn:art_8__para_8-2
GIVEN a IS AN `age-hours teacher`
GIVETH A LIST OF `age reduction`
DECIDE `the reductions section 8.2 gives` a IS
    IF a's `age for age hours` AT LEAST 50 AND a's `age for age hours` AT MOST 55
    THEN LIST `age reduction` 2 0 34
    ELSE EMPTY

@ref akn:art_8__para_8-3
GIVEN a IS AN `age-hours teacher`
GIVETH A LIST OF `age reduction`
DECIDE `the reductions section 8.3 gives` a IS
    IF a's `existing` AND a's `age for age hours` AT LEAST 55
    THEN LIST `age reduction` 3 1 32
    ELSE EMPTY

@ref akn:art_8__para_8-4 akn:art_8__para_8-4/p2
GIVEN a IS AN `age-hours teacher`
GIVETH A LIST OF `age reduction`
DECIDE `the reductions section 8.4 gives` a IS
    IF (NOT a's `existing`) AND a's `age for age hours` AT LEAST 55
    THEN LIST `age reduction` 2 0 34
    ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN a IS AN `age-hours teacher`
GIVETH A LIST OF `age reduction`
DECIDE `the reductions the text gives` a IS
    concat (LIST `the reductions section 8.2 gives` a,
                 `the reductions section 8.3 gives` a,
                 `the reductions section 8.4 gives` a)

-- F-2021-22_tashpab_02-d: an existing teacher aged 55 is in both 8.2
-- ("בגילאי 55-50") and 8.3 ("55 ומעלה").
`an existing teacher aged 55 gets two reductions` MEANS
    count (`the reductions the text gives` (`age-hours teacher` 55 TRUE)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `an existing teacher aged 55 gets two reductions`

-- The reading adopted: the band that opens at 55 governs 55. Part-time:
-- in proportion to the position.
GIVEN a IS AN `age-hours teacher`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `frontal hours off for age` a f IS
    IF a's `age for age hours` AT LEAST 55
    THEN IF a's `existing` THEN 3 TIMES f ELSE 2 TIMES f
    ELSE IF a's `age for age hours` AT LEAST 50 THEN 2 TIMES f ELSE 0

§§ `9 מבנה שבוע העבודה למנהלים וסגנים ראשונים`

-- 9.1: a principal and a first deputy work exactly 100%, five days.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-1
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a principal's or first deputy's position is lawful` `position fraction` IF
    `position fraction` EQUALS 1

-- 9.2-9.4: the principal works 40 hours, 6 to 9 of them frontal by the
-- school's complexity level; 8 levels by the school management index, the
-- minimum in special education being 3.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-2 akn:art_9__para_9-3 akn:art_9__para_9-4
`the principal's weekly hours` MEANS 40
`the minimum complexity level in special education` MEANS 3

-- 9.5-9.6: computed in early May of the previous school year from the
-- Ministry's data; a new institution's in December, the minimum level
-- applying until then and the result retroactive to the start of the year.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-5 akn:art_9__para_9-6
GIVEN `existed in May of the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN, `level computed in May` IS A NUMBER, `level computed in December` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the complexity level for the year` `existed in May of the previous year` `level computed in May` `level computed in December` IS
    IF `existed in May of the previous year`
    THEN max `the minimum complexity level in special education` `level computed in May`
    ELSE max `the minimum complexity level in special education` `level computed in December`

@desc A row of the complexity tables: the level and the frontal teaching hours.
DECLARE `complexity row` HAS
    `complexity level`      IS A NUMBER
    `frontal teaching hours` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-6/p2 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p3 akn:art_9__para_9-6/t1 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p4 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p5
`the principal's frontal hours by complexity` MEANS
    LIST `complexity row` 3 9, `complexity row` 4 8, `complexity row` 5 8,
         `complexity row` 6 7, `complexity row` 7 7, `complexity row` 8 6

-- 9.7: the first deputy works 40 hours, frontal hours by the school and
-- its level.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7
`the first deputy's weekly hours` MEANS 40

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-1 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-1/t1
`the primary first deputy's frontal hours by complexity` MEANS
    LIST `complexity row` 3 21, `complexity row` 4 21, `complexity row` 5 20,
         `complexity row` 6 20, `complexity row` 7 19, `complexity row` 8 18

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-2 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-2/t1
`the secondary first deputy's frontal hours by complexity` MEANS
    LIST `complexity row` 3 11, `complexity row` 4 11, `complexity row` 5 11,
         `complexity row` 6 11, `complexity row` 7 9, `complexity row` 8 9

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-3 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-3/t1
`the multi-stage first deputy's frontal hours by complexity` MEANS
    LIST `complexity row` 3 15, `complexity row` 4 15, `complexity row` 5 14,
         `complexity row` 6 14, `complexity row` 7 13, `complexity row` 8 13

GIVEN tbl IS A LIST OF `complexity row`
      lvl IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `frontal hours at level` tbl lvl IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `frontal teaching hours`) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `complexity level` EQUALS lvl) tbl))

-- Each table stays inside the range its clause states (6-9, 18-21, 9-11,
-- 13-15) and gives every level 3-8 one row.
GIVEN tbl  IS A LIST OF `complexity row`
      low  IS A NUMBER
      high IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the table fits its range` tbl low high IF
        all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `frontal teaching hours` AT LEAST low AND r's `frontal teaching hours` AT MOST high) tbl
    AND all (GIVEN l YIELD count (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `complexity level` EQUALS l) tbl) EQUALS 1) (range 3 8)

#ASSERT `the table fits its range` `the principal's frontal hours by complexity` 6 9
#ASSERT `the table fits its range` `the primary first deputy's frontal hours by complexity` 18 21
#ASSERT `the table fits its range` `the secondary first deputy's frontal hours by complexity` 9 11
#ASSERT `the table fits its range` `the multi-stage first deputy's frontal hours by complexity` 13 15

-- 9.8: a second deputy and after works a teacher's week; the individual
-- hours go to the deputy's work.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-8
GIVEN s IS A `school structure`, `teaches in grades 1-6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `a second deputy's week` s `teaches in grades 1-6` IS
    `the full-position work week` s `teaches in grades 1-6` FALSE

-- 9.9-9.10: a mother, and anyone aged 50 or more, among principals and
-- first deputies: two weekly hours off the non-frontal hours, position and
-- pay unchanged.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-9 akn:art_9__para_9-10
GIVEN `entitled to a mother's position` IS A BOOLEAN, `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `non-frontal hours off for a principal or first deputy` `entitled to a mother's position` `age` IS
    (IF `entitled to a mother's position` THEN 2 ELSE 0)
        PLUS (IF `age` AT LEAST 50 THEN 2 ELSE 0)

§§ `10 שעות פעילות בית ספרית`

-- 10.1-10.2: paid on top of the position, by the school's needs, up to 18
-- an half-year. 10.3: the purposes and their caps.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-1 akn:art_10__para_10-2
`activity hours a half-year, at most` MEANS 18

@desc The purposes §10.3 lists.
DECLARE `activity purpose` IS ONE OF
    `a general school meeting`
    `an individual parents' and children's meeting`
    `an after-school activity`

@ref akn:art_10__para_10-3 akn:art_10__para_10-3/p2 akn:art_10__para_10-3/p3 akn:art_10__para_10-3/p4
GIVEN p IS AN `activity purpose`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `activity hours a half-year for` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a general school meeting` THEN 4
    WHEN `an individual parents' and children's meeting` THEN 8
    WHEN `an after-school activity` THEN 6

`the purposes' caps add up to the half-year cap` MEANS
    sum (map `activity hours a half-year for` (LIST `a general school meeting`, `an individual parents' and children's meeting`, `an after-school activity`))
        EQUALS `activity hours a half-year, at most`
#ASSERT `the purposes' caps add up to the half-year cap`

§§ `11 יציאה מאופק חדש`

-- 11.1: everyone who meets the conditions joins. 11.2: exceptionally, a
-- request to leave may be heard for health (the teacher's or a
-- first-degree relative's, with current medical papers) or humanitarian
-- reasons (a change for the worse after joining). 11.3-11.4: on annex ד's
-- form, through the portal.
@desc The grounds §11.2 names.
DECLARE `ground for leaving` IS ONE OF
    `health of the teacher or a first-degree relative, with current medical papers`
    `a change for the worse in personal or family circumstances since joining`
    `another ground`

@ref akn:art_11__para_11-1 akn:art_11__para_11-2 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p2 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p3 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p4 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p5 akn:art_11__para_11-3 akn:art_11__para_11-4 akn:art_11__para_11-4/p2
GIVEN g IS A `ground for leaving`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a request to leave may be heard` g IF
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `another ground` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `12 קידום בדרגות`

-- 12.1: promotion needs the required period (פז"נ), professional-development
-- hours (שפ"מ) and an evaluation, by the Ministry's guidance and links.
@desc A promotion step: from grade, required months, development hours, and the supplement to the table salary.
DECLARE `promotion step` HAS
    `from grade`                IS A NUMBER
    `required months`           IS A NUMBER
    `development hours`         IS A NUMBER
    `supplement to table salary` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_12__para_12-1 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p6 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p7 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p8 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p9
GIVEN s IS A `promotion step`, months IS A NUMBER, hours IS A NUMBER, `evaluation passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step is earned` s months hours `evaluation passed` IF
        months AT LEAST s's `required months`
    AND hours AT LEAST s's `development hours`
    AND `evaluation passed`

-- akn:art_12__para_12-2/p1 The heading "12.2 promotion of teachers"; no rule.

-- 12.2.1: certified academics.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/t1
`promotion of certified academics` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` 1 30 120 0.075, `promotion step` 2 30 120 0.075,
         `promotion step` 3 36 180 0.075, `promotion step` 4 36 180 0.075,
         `promotion step` 5 36 180 0.075, `promotion step` 6 48 210 0.075,
         `promotion step` 7 48 210 0.075, `promotion step` 8 48 210 0.075

-- 12.2.2: uncertified academics. Veterans with seniority "עד 25 שנה" who
-- joined by exception are not promoted until certified; then the period and
-- hours count from joining, for one promotion only, and up to 60 study hours
-- count as development hours. Those with "25 שנה ומעלה" need no
-- certificate. New teachers joining by exception: no promotion until
-- certified, no benefits, counting from certification.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p6 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p7
GIVEN `years of seniority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `what section 12.2.2 says of an uncertified veteran` `years of seniority` IS
    append (IF `years of seniority` AT MOST 25 THEN LIST "no promotion until certified" ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF `years of seniority` AT LEAST 25 THEN LIST "promoted without a certificate" ELSE EMPTY)

`study hours that may count as development hours, at most` MEANS 60

-- F-2021-22_tashpab_02-e: at exactly 25 years 12.2.2 says both; §3.2.1 ¶10
-- says "below 25".
`at 25 years section 12.2.2 gives both answers` MEANS
    count (`what section 12.2.2 says of an uncertified veteran` 25) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `at 25 years section 12.2.2 gives both answers`

-- The reading adopted: §3.2.1's "below 25" — 25 years need no certificate.
GIVEN `years of seniority` IS A NUMBER, `certified to teach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an academic may be promoted` `years of seniority` `certified to teach` IF
        `certified to teach`
    OR  `years of seniority` AT LEAST 25

-- 12.2.3: certified non-academics. Up to 27 years: the commitment of §3.3
-- and no promotion until the degree; 28 years or more: no degree needed,
-- and the slower table.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/t1
`promotion of non-academics with 28 years` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` 1 48 480 0.075, `promotion step` 2 48 480 0.075,
         `promotion step` 3 48 480 0.075, `promotion step` 4 48 480 0.075,
         `promotion step` 5 48 480 0.075, `promotion step` 6 48 480 0.075,
         `promotion step` 7 48 480 0.075, `promotion step` 8 48 480 0.075

GIVEN `years of seniority` IS A NUMBER, `completed the degree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a non-academic may be promoted` `years of seniority` `completed the degree` IF
        `completed the degree`
    OR  `years of seniority` AT LEAST 28

-- akn:art_12__para_12-3/p1 The heading "12.3 promotion of principals and deputies"; no rule.

-- 12.3: principals and deputies, grades א'-ד' (1-4 here).
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/t1
`promotion of certified academic principals and deputies` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` 1 36 210 0.0875, `promotion step` 2 36 210 0.0875, `promotion step` 3 36 210 0.0875

@ref akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/t1
`promotion of non-academic principals and deputies with 28 years` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` 1 48 480 0.0875, `promotion step` 2 48 480 0.0875, `promotion step` 3 48 480 0.0875

§§ `13 יועצים חינוכיים`

-- 13.1: a counsellor's week is an academic teacher's, the frontal hours
-- split by the principal between teaching and counselling, the individual
-- hours counselling, the stay hours a teacher's and for counselling too;
-- at least a sixth of the position (6 of 36) frontal teaching in primary
-- and junior-high schools, and at least 4 frontal hours a position.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-1 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p4 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p5 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p6 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p7 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p8 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p9
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a counsellor's minimum frontal teaching hours` `position fraction` IS
    max (36 TIMES `position fraction` DIVIDED BY 6) 4

-- 13.2: new counsellors are on the new academic teachers' tables.
-- 13.3: a counsellor with at least 7 counselling hours gets a counselling
-- bonus: 8% on a temporary licence, 12% on a permanent one.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-2 akn:art_13__para_13-3 akn:art_13__para_13-3/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-3/p3
GIVEN `counselling hours` IS A NUMBER, `permanent licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the counselling bonus rate` `counselling hours` `permanent licence` IS
    IF `counselling hours` AT LEAST 7
    THEN IF `permanent licence` THEN 0.12 ELSE 0.08
    ELSE 0

§§ `14 קביעת הדרגה באופק חדש`

-- 14.1-14.5: the Ministry alone sets the grade, from employment, education
-- and salary data; the conversion uses the March salary of the year before
-- joining at 100% by the roles; the grade may be a half grade.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-1 akn:art_14__para_14-2 akn:art_14__para_14-3 akn:art_14__para_14-4 akn:art_14__para_14-5
GIVEN `grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a grade the conversion may give` `grade` IF
    `grade` TIMES 2 EQUALS FLOOR (`grade` TIMES 2)

-- akn:art_14__para_14-6 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p4 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p5 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p6 More information to follow, annex ה's explanation, and links to the salary tables and the 2016 shekel-supplement circular; the conversion is encoded with annex ה below.

-- 14.7: the role bonuses under Ofek Hadash, at most two to a teacher.
@desc The roles §14.7 lists.
DECLARE `role` IS ONE OF
    `second deputy principal`
    `homeroom teacher`
    `first-grade homeroom teacher`
    `subject coordinator in a primary school`
    `subject coordinator in a junior high school`
    `road-safety coordinator`
    `security coordinator`
    `social education in a primary school`
    `social education in a junior high school`
    `grade coordinator`
    `laboratory coordinator`
    `measurement and evaluation coordinator`
    `trips coordinator`
    `inclusion coordinator`
    `pedagogical coordinator`

-- "רכז שכבה* 7% / 6%": the asterisk's note is not in the corpus text, so
-- which of the two rates applies is an input (see the hand-off).
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p4 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p6 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p7 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p8 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p9 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p10 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p11 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p12 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p13 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p14 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p15
GIVEN r IS A `role`, `grade coordinator's rate` IS A NUMBER @desc 0.06 or 0.07, by the note the asterisk points to
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the role bonus rate` r `grade coordinator's rate` IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `second deputy principal` THEN 0.13
    WHEN `homeroom teacher` THEN 0.10
    WHEN `first-grade homeroom teacher` THEN 0.115
    WHEN `subject coordinator in a primary school` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `subject coordinator in a junior high school` THEN 0.08
    WHEN `road-safety coordinator` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `security coordinator` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `social education in a primary school` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `social education in a junior high school` THEN 0.10
    WHEN `grade coordinator` THEN `grade coordinator's rate`
    WHEN `laboratory coordinator` THEN 0.03
    WHEN `measurement and evaluation coordinator` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `trips coordinator` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `inclusion coordinator` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `pedagogical coordinator` THEN 0.06

-- The special-education supplement "as customary today" is set outside the
-- circular (an input); the mentor's is 2.4% an intern, up to three.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7/p5
GIVEN `the special-education rate customary today` IS A NUMBER @desc the special-education rate as paid today, which the circular does not state
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the special-education rate` `the special-education rate customary today` IS
    `the special-education rate customary today`

@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7/p16
GIVEN interns IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the mentor's bonus rate` interns IS
    0.024 TIMES min interns 3

@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7/p17
`role bonuses a teacher may hold, at most` MEANS 2

GIVEN roles IS A LIST OF `role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the roles may all carry a bonus` roles IF
    count roles AT MOST `role bonuses a teacher may hold, at most`

§§ `15 מקדמות שכר באופק חדש עד לקביעת הדרגה`

-- 15.1: until the grade is set, the owner pays a teacher who joined an
-- advance on top of the current (pre-reform) salary, computed on the
-- components listed, for the part of the employment in the school that
-- joined and from the joining date; named "מקדמת אופק חדש". After the
-- grade is set, the Ofek salary is paid back to the joining date and the
-- salary and advances paid are set off.
@desc The salary components §15.1 computes the advance on.
DECLARE `advance component` IS ONE OF
    `combined salary`, `supplement`, `supplement 87`, `supplement 94`, `supplement 2001`,
    `supplement 2008`, `split-day bonus`, `in-service training bonuses`, `double-degree bonus`,
    `supplement 2011`

@desc The rows of §15.2.
DECLARE `advance group` IS ONE OF
    `primary or grades 1-6, not a principal or first deputy`
    `primary or grades 1-6, an intern`
    `secondary or grades 7 and up, not a principal or first deputy`
    `secondary or grades 7 and up, an intern`
    `a first deputy`
    `a principal`

@ref akn:art_15__para_15-2 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p3 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p4 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p5 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p6 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p7 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p8 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p9 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p10
GIVEN g IS AN `advance group`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance rate` g IS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `primary or grades 1-6, not a principal or first deputy` THEN 0.17
    WHEN `primary or grades 1-6, an intern` THEN 0.14
    WHEN `secondary or grades 7 and up, not a principal or first deputy` THEN 0.27
    WHEN `secondary or grades 7 and up, an intern` THEN 0.22
    WHEN `a first deputy` THEN 0.20
    WHEN `a principal` THEN 0.15

@ref akn:art_15__para_15-1 akn:art_15__para_15-1/p2
GIVEN g IS AN `advance group`
      `the listed components of the current salary` IS A NUMBER @desc the sum of the current salary's components §15.1 lists, for the part of the employment in the school that joined
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ofek Hadash advance` g `the listed components of the current salary` IS
    `the advance rate` g TIMES `the listed components of the current salary`

@ref akn:art_15__para_15-1/p3
GIVEN `Ofek salary from joining` IS A NUMBER, `salary paid from joining` IS A NUMBER, `advances paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the arrears once the grade is set` `Ofek salary from joining` `salary paid from joining` `advances paid` IS
    `Ofek salary from joining` MINUS (`salary paid from joining` PLUS `advances paid`)

-- akn:art_15/p1 The reimbursement for the advance will be set out in a separate circular; no rule here.

§§ `16 שעון הנוכחות בביה"ס`

-- 16.1-16.3: a time clock is installed and the teachers report on it,
-- manually until it is; hours count from the punch and not before 7:45.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-1 akn:art_16__para_16-2 akn:art_16__para_16-3
GIVEN `punch time in minutes after midnight` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the working day starts at` `punch time in minutes after midnight` IS
    max `punch time in minutes after midnight` (7 TIMES 60 PLUS 45)

-- 16.4: the owner pays and deducts by the clock's data, after checking
-- justified absences (sickness, mourning and the like).
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-4/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `paying by the time clock` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay and deduct salary by the time clock`

-- §17 (printed inside 16.4 in the corpus): the circular gathers the
-- agreements' rules, and where it contradicts them, for or against the
-- employee, the agreements prevail.
@desc The instruments §17 ranks.
DECLARE `instrument` IS ONE OF
    `this circular`
    `the collective agreements on Ofek Hadash`

@ref akn:art_16__para_16-4/p2
GIVEN `what the circular says` IS A NUMBER, `what the agreements say` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rule that applies` `what the circular says` `what the agreements say` IS
    `what the agreements say`

-- akn:art_16__para_16-4/p3 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p4 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p5 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p6 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p7 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p8 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p9 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p10 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p11 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p12 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p13 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p14 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p15 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p16 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p17 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p18 The sign-off and the first copies, which the corpus prints inside §16.4; no rule.
-- akn:art_16__para_16-4/p19 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p20 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p21 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p22 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p23 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p24 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p25 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p26 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p27 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p28 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p29 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p30 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p31 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p32 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p33 The rest of the list of copies; no rule.

§§ `נספח א' כתב התחייבות`

-- The owner's commitment: from תשפ"ב, to apply to the special-education
-- schools it owns every provision of the Ofek Hadash agreement of
-- 25.12.2008 as updated that concerns them — the work week, the pay and
-- the pedagogical guidance — on pain of sanctions up to the revocation of
-- the licence.
@desc What the commitment binds the owner to.
DECLARE `committed matter` IS ONE OF
    `the Ofek Hadash work week`
    `pay by Ofek Hadash`
    `the pedagogical guidance on Ofek Hadash`

@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1/p4
GIVEN m IS A `committed matter`, `applied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is exposed to sanctions up to revocation of the licence` m `applied` IF
    NOT `applied`

-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1/p5 akn:att_1__hc_1/p6 akn:att_1__hc_1/p7 akn:att_1__hc_1/p8 akn:att_1__hc_1/p9 akn:att_1__hc_1/p10 akn:att_1__hc_1/p11 The form's fields: the signatory, the owner, the schools covered and the signature lines; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p12 akn:att_1__hc_1/p13 akn:att_1__hc_1/p14 akn:att_1__hc_1/p15 The page's letterhead; no rule.

§§ `נספח ב' בקשה להצטרפות חריגה`

-- The exceptional-joining form of an academic without a teaching
-- certificate: the teacher acknowledges no promotion until certified
-- (§3.2.1, encoded above) and that the reform's terms apply on signing.
@ref akn:att_2__hc_1/p10 akn:att_2__hc_1/p11
GIVEN `signed the exceptional-joining form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reform's terms apply on signing the exceptional-joining form` `signed the exceptional-joining form` IF
    `signed the exceptional-joining form`

-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p1 akn:att_2__hc_1/p2 akn:att_2__hc_1/p3 akn:att_2__hc_1/p4 akn:att_2__hc_1/p5 akn:att_2__hc_1/p6 akn:att_2__hc_1/p7 akn:att_2__hc_1/p8 akn:att_2__hc_1/p9 The form's title and fields; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p12 akn:att_2__hc_1/p13 akn:att_2__hc_1/p14 akn:att_2__hc_1/p15 akn:att_2__hc_1/p16 akn:att_2__hc_1/p17 akn:att_2__hc_1/p18 The signature line, the portal link and the page's letterhead; no rule.

§§ `נספח ג' התחייבות להשלמת תואר`

-- The non-academic teacher's commitment: to complete the degree within 4
-- years of SIGNING (¶9); completed within 4 years of JOINING, arrears back
-- to the date of SIGNING (¶10). F-2021-22_tashpab_02-f: §3.3.4 counts the
-- window from joining and pays the arrears from joining.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1/p9 akn:att_3__hc_1/p10
GIVEN `months from signing to the degree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the degree is within the commitment's window` `months from signing to the degree` IF
    `months from signing to the degree` AT MOST 48

-- A teacher who joined with the school at the start of the year, signed the
-- commitment four months later (§3.3.1 is satisfied on signing; the circular
-- sets no date for it), and completes the degree 47 months after signing —
-- 51 months after joining.
`months from joining to signing` MEANS 4
`months from signing to completion` MEANS 47

`section 3.3.4 and annex ג decide the same teacher differently` MEANS
        `the degree is within the commitment's window` `months from signing to completion`
    AND (NOT `arrears from joining under section 3.3.4` (`months from joining to signing` PLUS `months from signing to completion`))
#ASSERT `section 3.3.4 and annex ג decide the same teacher differently`

-- The reading adopted: §3.3.4, which the circular states as the rule, and
-- annex ג's ¶10, which states the same test, both count from joining; the
-- arrears run from joining (§3.3.4). ¶11-16 define an academic degree:
-- an Israeli degree recognised by the Council for Higher Education, a
-- foreign degree recognised as equivalent, or studies the division approved
-- as an equivalent grade (§3.2.1's `academic`).
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1/p11 akn:att_3__hc_1/p12 akn:att_3__hc_1/p13 akn:att_3__hc_1/p14 akn:att_3__hc_1/p15 akn:att_3__hc_1/p16 akn:att_3__hc_1/p17 akn:att_3__hc_1/p18
GIVEN `Israeli degree recognised by the Council for Higher Education` IS A BOOLEAN
      `foreign degree recognised as equivalent`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `studies approved as an equivalent grade`                    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an academic degree for annex ג` `Israeli degree recognised by the Council for Higher Education` `foreign degree recognised as equivalent` `studies approved as an equivalent grade` IF
        `Israeli degree recognised by the Council for Higher Education`
    OR  `foreign degree recognised as equivalent`
    OR  `studies approved as an equivalent grade`

-- akn:att_3__hc_1/p1 akn:att_3__hc_1/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1/p3 akn:att_3__hc_1/p4 akn:att_3__hc_1/p5 akn:att_3__hc_1/p6 akn:att_3__hc_1/p7 akn:att_3__hc_1/p8 The form's title and fields; no rule.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1/p19 akn:att_3__hc_1/p20 akn:att_3__hc_1/p21 akn:att_3__hc_1/p22 akn:att_3__hc_1/p23 akn:att_3__hc_1/p24 akn:att_3__hc_1/p25 The signature line, the portal link and the page's letterhead; no rule.

§§ `נספח ד' בקשה ליציאה מהרפורמה`

-- akn:att_4__hc_1 The form for asking the exceptions committee to leave the reform (§§11.2-11.4, encoded there): its title, fields, the principal's comment line, the portal link and letterhead; no rule of its own.

§§ `נספח ה' קביעת דרגה והמרות שכר`

-- ¶1-5: an existing teacher's grade is set by converting the salary, by
-- personal data, roles and stage; a new teacher is placed at grade 1 with
-- no conversion; the Ministry alone sets grades.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1/p5
GIVEN t IS AN `Ofek teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the salary is converted` t IF
    `an existing teaching employee` t

-- 1א: the formula: A = X × (100 + Y)%.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p6 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_c akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_c/p2
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary after conversion` x y IS
    x TIMES ((100 PLUS y) DIVIDED BY 100)

-- 1ב: X is the salary the teacher was entitled to at 100% by the roles,
-- in March of the year before joining (the joining month if not employed in
-- March), from the components listed and the role bonuses that do not go on.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p6
GIVEN `components at the position held` IS A NUMBER, `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary to convert` `components at the position held` `position fraction` IS
    `components at the position held` DIVIDED BY `position fraction`

-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p7 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p8 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p9 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p10 The page's letterhead; no rule.

-- ¶11-14: the coefficients. ¶11 heads the academic teachers' coefficients,
-- but the corpus carries no table under it (a corpus defect: see the
-- hand-off), so the academic coefficient is an input. A non-academic's is
-- the academic's times 0.8; a primary-school teacher of grades 7-9 on a
-- 24-hour base gets 12.5% more (and works the primary week).
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p11 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p12 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p13 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p14
GIVEN `the academic coefficient` IS A NUMBER @desc the conversion coefficient for an academic teacher in the teacher's case, from the table the corpus does not carry
      `academic` IS A BOOLEAN
      `primary teacher of grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the conversion coefficient` `the academic coefficient` `academic` `primary teacher of grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` IS
    (IF `academic` THEN `the academic coefficient` ELSE `the academic coefficient` TIMES 0.8)
        TIMES (IF `primary teacher of grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` THEN 1.125 ELSE 1)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `to the agora` x IS
    ROUND (x TIMES 100) DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `truncated to the agora` x IS
    TRUNC x 2

-- The example (¶15-31 and 1ג): a mother, an academic with a first degree,
-- in a junior high school at 0.9 of a position. The components it lists:
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p15 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p16 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p17 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p18 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p19 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p20 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p21 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p22 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p23 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p24 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p25 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p26 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p27 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p28
`the teacher example's components` MEANS
    LIST 3779.38, 141.21, 113.38, 187.25, 259.08, 157.03, 268.82, 900.54, 298.69

#ASSERT sum `the teacher example's components` EQUALS 6105.38

-- ¶29: X = 6,105.38 / 0.9 = 6,783.75 (truncated to the agora).
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p29
`the teacher example's X` MEANS
    `truncated to the agora` (`the salary to convert` (sum `the teacher example's components`) 0.9)

#ASSERT `the teacher example's X` EQUALS 6783.75

-- ¶30: the example multiplies X by 1.034, "תוספת שחיקה" (an erosion
-- supplement), which neither the formula (1א) nor the definition of X (1ב)
-- mentions. ¶31: Y = 34. 1ג: A = 9,399.29.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p30 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p31
`the erosion supplement the examples apply` MEANS 1.034

`the teacher example's printed A` MEANS 9399.29

-- The example's A is reproduced with the erosion supplement, carried
-- unrounded from the printed X ...
#ASSERT `to the agora` (`the salary after conversion` (`the teacher example's X` TIMES `the erosion supplement the examples apply`) 34) EQUALS `the teacher example's printed A`

-- ... and F-2021-22_tashpab_02-g: not by the formula the annex states.
`the conversion examples apply a supplement the formula does not state` MEANS
    NOT (`to the agora` (`the salary after conversion` `the teacher example's X` 34) EQUALS `the teacher example's printed A`)
#ASSERT `the conversion examples apply a supplement the formula does not state`

-- 1ד: placed on the academic table by total seniority, at the grade whose
-- salary is nearest A, equal to it or higher. The example: seniority 10
-- (8 teaching years + 21 months' military service), salary ₪9,670.70,
-- grade 6. The tables are not in the circular (an input).
@desc A cell of an Ofek Hadash salary table at the teacher's seniority: the grade and its salary.
DECLARE `table cell` HAS
    `cell grade`  IS A NUMBER
    `cell salary` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p4
GIVEN cells IS A LIST OF `table cell`
      a     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `table cell`
DECIDE `the cells at or above A` cells a IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `cell salary` AT LEAST a) cells

#ASSERT 9670.70 AT LEAST `the teacher example's printed A`

-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p5 The heading "דגשים"; no rule.

-- Notes 1-2: a new academic (after the internship) is placed at grade 1
-- and seniority 1 without conversion; one on unpaid leave, sabbatical or
-- unpaid absence in the year before joining is converted on the salary
-- that would have been paid for September of the joining year.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_2
GIVEN `on unpaid absence in the year before joining` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the month the salary to convert is taken from` `on unpaid absence in the year before joining` IS
    IF `on unpaid absence in the year before joining`
    THEN "September of the year of joining"
    ELSE "March of the school year before joining"

-- 2: first deputies. 2א-ב: Y = 20%. 2ג: X is the salary, except the
-- homeroom bonus, expense refunds, sundry payments, tax gross-up and taxable
-- benefits, at 100% in March before the move (September if absent).
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p3
`the first deputy's coefficient` MEANS 20

-- The deputy example: an academic deputy in a junior high school at
